# Database Safety & Multi-Tenant Architecture

**CRITICAL:** One mistake here can expose client data across tenants.

## Hard Constraints

```sql
-- NEVER disable RLS on tenant-scoped tables
ALTER TABLE workspaces DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;  -- FORBIDDEN

-- NEVER query without tenant context
SELECT * FROM people;  -- DANGEROUS

-- ALWAYS include tenant scoping
SELECT * FROM people
WHERE workspace_id IN (
  SELECT workspace_id FROM workspace_members WHERE user_id = auth.uid()
);
```

## RLS Patterns

### Workspace Member Access (Most Common)
```sql
CREATE POLICY "policy_name" ON table_name
FOR operation USING (
  workspace_id IN (
    SELECT workspace_id FROM workspace_members
    WHERE user_id = auth.uid()
  )
);
```

### Role-Based Access
```sql
CREATE POLICY "admins_can_manage" ON workspace_members
FOR ALL USING (
  workspace_id IN (
    SELECT workspace_id FROM workspace_members
    WHERE user_id = auth.uid()
    AND role IN ('owner', 'admin')
  )
);
```

## Safe Migration Pattern

```sql
-- New tenant-scoped table
CREATE TABLE new_table (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  workspace_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX new_table_workspace_id_idx ON new_table(workspace_id);
ALTER TABLE new_table ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "workspace_members_can_view" ON new_table
FOR SELECT USING (
  workspace_id IN (
    SELECT workspace_id FROM workspace_members WHERE user_id = auth.uid()
  )
);
```

## Pre-Deploy Checklist

- [ ] RLS Enabled on all new tables
- [ ] Policies created (at least SELECT)
- [ ] Foreign keys have ON DELETE CASCADE
- [ ] Tenant boundary columns indexed
- [ ] Rollback SQL written and tested
